1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
 No quant team, no code, just the new Jeff model.

2
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:08,520
 Here's what happened, how I built it, and how you can copy it.

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:12,340
 I started with $50,000, and in five days, I was up 20%.

4
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:13,700
 Now, let me show you how it's done.

5
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,080
 First, what is Jeff?

6
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,640
 ChatGPT is built to talk.

7
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:19,360
 You ask it a question, and it gives you back a paragraph.

8
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:21,500
 Jeff is built to decide.

9
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:23,480
 Think of it like a multiple choice question.

10
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,340
 You give it a clear set of questions and answers

11
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:29,100
 and can choose from buy, sell, or hold.

12
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:32,080
 It will make a decision and give you a confident score.

13
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:34,460
 Something like buy 82% sure.

14
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,700
 It can only choose from your list, so it can't make something up.

15
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,240
 And it answers in just half a second.

16
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:46,000
 It was built by Diogo Almeida when the researchers behind ChatGPT

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,700
 just launched, and the developers are going crazy over it.

18
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:50,940
 Why does this matter for trading?

19
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:54,100
 Think of a stock going up 8% in just one minute.

20
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:57,300
 By the time you ask ChatGPT, that stock has already moved.

21
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,240
 But Jeff can make a decision in milliseconds.

22
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:02,800
 So, I plug it into my own trading account.

23
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:03,580
 Three pieces.

24
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:05,540
 One, TKO exposed the strategy.

25
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:10,360
 I describe my strategy in plain English, and it creates a set of clear rules.

26
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:14,140
 Then, it back-tests them on years of market data

27
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:20,580
 and stress-test them on trading fees, slippage, and market conditions where the strategy no longer works.

28
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:22,120
 Two, Jeff makes the call.

29
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:26,840
 Every time new market data comes in, Jeff checks against my clear set of rules

30
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:30,160
 and decides buy, sell, or hold with a confidence score.

31
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:35,520
 Three, TKOX trades through my broker inside the risk limits I set,

32
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:38,820
 like how much I'm willing to lose in one day, then I stay out of the way.

33
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:40,360
 That's where the number comes from.

34
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,820
 Rules and discipline.

35
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,080
 Not a gut feeling.

36
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,420
 Comment, Jeff, and I'll send you the full setup.

